  "summary": "Omics studies increasingly treat goal definition, decomposition, and model transfer as testable modeling choices rather than fixed defaults.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that structural modeling decisions are specified and evaluated rather than inherited. GD-SI defines sepsis subgroups against an explicit goal across longitudinal multi-omics data from 1327 patients. cvaNMF wraps cross-validation around NMF for compositional signature decomposition, with benchmarks on synthetic data. The vaccine reactogenicity study fits a penalized ordinal regression across species and compartments on BioVacSafe transcriptomes. Ember applies Shannon's chain rule to score gene specificity in single-cell RNA-seq, and the disease network study adds STRING node2vec embeddings to omics data, recovering 2-4x more known disease proteins. The IBD study models cumulative non-coding SNP effects on signalling and gene regulatory networks. HGMT is a data resource rather than a modeling comparison and sits at the periphery. What is new is treating goal definition, decomposition, and model transfer as objects of evaluation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
